Records of the consent choices you make in our cookie banner are kept for {{CONSENT_RECORD_RETENTION}} from collection, so that we can demonstrate the consent we rely on. Other data collected through cookies — including analytics data — is kept only for as long as its purpose requires and, where no shorter cookie-specific period is shown, for no longer than the declared fallback period of {{RETENTION_PERIOD}}. Strictly necessary cookies are retained only for the duration of the session or as required for the technical function they serve. See the table above for the specific lifetime of each cookie.',
			'Cookie policy template: turkey-kvkk / section-7',
			'faz-cookie-manager'
		),
		_x(
			'## 8. Your rights under Article 11 and how to apply

As a data subject, you have the following rights under Article 11 of the Law:

- to learn whether your personal data is processed, and to request information about it;
- to learn the purpose of processing and whether your data is used in line with that purpose;
- to know the third parties, in Türkiye or abroad, to whom your personal data is transferred;
- to request rectification of incomplete or incorrectly processed personal data;
- to request erasure or destruction of your personal data where the reasons for processing have ceased, even if processed lawfully under the Law and other applicable statutes;
- to request that such rectification and erasure/destruction be notified to the third parties to whom your data was transferred;
- to object to the emergence of a result against you that is based exclusively on automated processing carried out through automatic systems;
- to claim compensation for damages arising from the unlawful processing of your personal data.

To exercise these rights, you may send an application containing the information required to identify you and clearly stating the right you invoke, by e-mail to **{{COMPANY_EMAIL}}** or by post to **{{COMPANY_ADDRESS}}**, fill in our form, or send it via registered electronic mail (KEP) or with a secure electronic signature. Your applications will be concluded as soon as possible and within thirty (30) days at the latest; if the transaction requires an additional cost, a fee may be charged according to the tariff set by the Personal Data Protection Board. In case your request is rejected, the response is found insufficient, or is not answered in time, you retain the right to lodge a complaint with the Board (the Personal Data Protection Authority) and to seek judicial review of Board decisions ({{OFFICIAL_RESOURCES_URL}}).',
